/T (Many economists in favour of remaining in the EU argued that Brexit would fundamentally damage the competitiveness of UK firms, as leaving the Single Market would result in a range of tariff and non-tariff barriers being imposed on UK firms exporting to EU countries. Those in favour of leaving the EU said that this would be outweighed by the gains that would come from negotiating free trade deals with non- EU countries, which would be easier to do once the UK left the trading bloc.)
/E (Many economists in favour of remaining in the EU argued that Brexit would fundamentally damage the competitiveness of UK firms, as leaving the Single Market would result in a range of tariff and non-tariff barriers being imposed on UK firms exporting to EU countries. Those in favour of leaving the EU said that this would be outweighed by the gains that would come from negotiating free trade deals with non- EU countries, which would be easier to do once the UK left the trading bloc.)
