/T (One of the main benefits Leave campaigners argued would result from leaving the European Union was the ability this would give the UK government to take control of its borders. They argued that rising immigration had put increasing pressure on public services, pushed house prices up and depressed the wages and employment opportunities for low skilled workers.)
