5305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (However, many economists argued the end of free movement presented many risks to the prosperity of the UK economy. Empirical evidence suggests that EU immigrants tend to be younger than the native population and more likely to work and pay taxes than claim benefits, in doing so addressing the problems an ageing population could cause the economy. Moreover, a number of industries such as healthcare and construction are reliant on immigrants to fill skills shortages, with immigration allowing the UK to benefit from greater labour market flexibility.)
/E (However, many economists argued the end of free movement presented many risks to the prosperity of the UK economy. Empirical evidence suggests that EU immigrants tend to be younger than the native population and more likely to work and pay taxes than claim benefits, in doing so addressing the problems an ageing population could cause the economy. Moreover, a number of industries such as healthcare and construction are reliant on immigrants to fill skills shortages, with immigration allowing the UK to benefit from greater labour market flexibility.)
/Pg 98 0 R
/K [4]
>>
