/S /H2
/T (World trade grew by 4.4% in 2017 and is predicted to grow by 4.7% in 2018. China is accounting for a higher proportion of this global trade and a higher proportion of global output. The country has experienced a significant rise in its GDP per head in recent years. This has had an impact on its citizens' life expectancy. Fig. 1 shows the average income and life expectancy in a number of countries.)
/E (World trade grew by 4.4% in 2017 and is predicted to grow by 4.7% in 2018. China is accounting for a higher proportion of this global trade and a higher proportion of global output. The country has experienced a significant rise in its GDP per head in recent years. This has had an impact on its citizens' life expectancy. Fig. 1 shows the average income and life expectancy in a number of countries.)
